---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site.config';
const email = siteConfig.org.contactEmail;
---
<BaseLayout title={`About ${siteConfig.identity.name}`} description="makepicsmall is a privacy-first image compressor. Files stay on your device — compression runs entirely in your browser via WebAssembly.">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">About {siteConfig.identity.name}</h1>
  <div class="prose prose-slate mt-6 max-w-none">
    <p class="lead">
      {siteConfig.identity.name} is a privacy-first image compressor.
      We think image tools shouldn't need your data to shrink a photo.
      That's the whole pitch.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every other compressor we tried uploaded your images to a server
      somewhere, ran them through a tool you could just as easily run
      locally, and sent the result back with a tracker attached. We
      rebuilt that flow the way it should have been in the first place:
      the compressor (built on <a href="https://github.com/jamsinclair/jSquash" rel="noopener">jSquash</a>,
      which wraps the same mozjpeg, oxipng, and libwebp codecs the pros
      use) runs inside your browser as WebAssembly. Your files never
      touch our servers because there is no server for them to touch —
      makepicsmall is a static site hosted on Cloudflare Pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      The result is fast (no round-trip to a server), safe (nothing to
      leak, because nothing was uploaded), and free (nothing to
      monetize, because we collect nothing). We hope it's useful.
    </p>
    <p>
      Found a bug, have a feature request, or want to say hi?
      Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
